            "review_title": "Review at Baozi",
            "review_text": "Jon R\nDa Nang, Vietnam3 contributions\n0\nQuality suffers post-covid\nAug 2022 • Family\nWent for lunch. We used to come now and again before COVID and used to really enjoy the food however our recent trip was quite disappointing. Service quality suffered greatly compared to pre-covid. Staff were loitering around not really paying attention, we had a tough time putting in our order or getting anything. Food was okay, some items on the menu have changed their recipie (make sure to ask if something is spicy as unexpected things will have chili thrown in). We tried the milk tea, which was a nice concept (the caramalized sugar on top was great) but ruined in execution since the grass jelly was a single large chunk literally half the size of the glass (were staff too lazy to cut it small? Is the concept to get an entire bowlful of jelly when you are expecting to order a drink?) \nAfter realizing the initial order wouldn't work for a member of our family we ordered a chicken rice to compensate and after waiting for a while for it to appear we were told it would take 15 minutes to prepare. I was quite in shock as is was just after 12. what restaurant doesn't prepare rice in advance of lunch rush??? Isn't rice one of the few things you can make in bulk and keep on hand??? (When asked if we could even change to white rice they said all the rice needed 15 min? What?) So we told the staff to cancel. Given their complete disorder staff predictably forgot to inform the kitchen, and so at the same time we asked for the bill the rice came. Sending the order back caused some confusion and they forgot to take our bill. Took another few minutes to catch their attention and pay. \nGiven the price, dealing with the complete chaos of the serving crew isn't really worth it.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 6, 2022",
