            "review_title": "Review at Baozi",
            "review_text": "Wandering Wheatleys\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam1731 contributions\n75\nOverall good food, but with a few cons...\nJan 2020 • Couples\nI’ll start with the pros... the food at Baozi is really really delicious and unique. The chicken ramen was by far the best dish we ordered followed by the wasabi chicken bao, then the duck poutine, and finally the pork belly bao which we were underwhelmed by. Flavors were incredibly rich and decadent, and although portion sizes weren’t huge, we left feeling full and satisfied. \n\nCan’t the cons... it’s pretty pricey, especially by Vietnamese standards. The pork bao we had tasted exactly like one we ordered from Bao Boi but it was 3 times the price. The ramen was 160k, the poutine was 135k, and all of the baos were in the 60-70k range. Plus they add VAT and service at the end. \n\nBut the REAL con and why they only get 3 stars was that they wouldn’t let us drink our own bottled water and they don’t offer glasses of water. So if you think you might get parched during your meal, you’ll be forced to purchase a small bottle of water for 23k. I’ve literally never been to a restaurant in Vietnam that won’t let you drink your own bottled water, especially when the food is so pricey but the ambiance isn’t fancy by any means. Plus I’m 9 months pregnant so it’s not like I’ve filled my Aquafina bottle with vodka. It’s a pretty lame rule and you should at the very least offer free glasses of water if you’re going to enforce it. It’s just bad customer service imho.\nRead more\nWritten January 9, 2020",
